    <MST.showAbstract>Show Default</MST.showAbstract>
    <MST.showAbstractTooltip>If the value is Null, whether to display the default value for the selected column. Note: The actual value is not changed.</MST.showAbstractTooltip>
    <MST.showChanged>Show Result</MST.showChanged>
    <MST.showChangedTooltip>Whether to display the result of applying global changes to the selected column. Note: The actual value is not changed.</MST.showChangedTooltip>
    <MST.showDisplayMode>Display Mode</MST.showDisplayMode>
    <MST.showDisplayModeTooltip>Display all cells in read-only mode. Editing is disabled.</MST.showDisplayModeTooltip>
    <MST.ResetColTooltip>Reset all data displayed in the currently selected column. Does not reset data not displayed in the list.</MST.ResetColTooltip>
    <MST.JumpToDesc>Click the name to jump to its associated data.</MST.JumpToDesc>
    <MST.ResetCurTooltip>Reset all data currently displayed. Does not reset data not displayed in the list.</MST.ResetCurTooltip>
    <MST.ApplyToolTip>Modify all values in the selected column. Only modifies data displayed in the current list. The result is (Value + Flat Change) * Multiplier.</MST.ApplyToolTip>
    <MST.HelpTooltip>Operations
- Top row: Apply = applies (value + flat) * multiplier to the visible data of the selected column, clamped by the lower/upper limits. Also: Columns / Settings / Reset Column / Reset Shown Items.
- Bottom row: search, main type / sub type / mod filters, sort. "Show Result" and "Show Default" only change the display, never the data; "Display Mode" makes the whole table read-only.
- Editing a cell: a checkbox toggles; number / percent values are typed in place; an enum opens a dropdown; text, lists, curves, def pickers and so on open their own editor window.
- Batch edit: hold Shift and drag with the left button to copy the start cell's value to every cell you drag over in the same column.
- Name column: left-click the name to jump to its owner; right-click for Pin / Reset / Copy defName; the R button resets that entry.
- Right-click a data cell: Copy / Paste / Reset that field.</MST.HelpTooltip>
